        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And the word of the Lord came unto him, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:2",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Get thee hence, and turn thee eastward, and hide thyself by the brook Cherith, that is before Jordan.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "1 Ne. 3:27; Mosiah 17:4 (1–4); Ether 13:13 (13, 22). TG Prophets, Rejection of."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "OR east of (also v. 5)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:3",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And it shall be, that thou shalt drink of the brook; and I have commanded the ravens to feed thee there.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:4",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "So he went and did according unto the word of the Lord: for he went and dwelt by the brook Cherith, that is before Jordan.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 107
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:5",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And the ravens brought him bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening; and he drank of the brook.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:6",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass after a while, that the brook dried up, because there had been no rain in the land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:7",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And the word of the Lord came unto him, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:8",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Arise, get thee to Zarephath, which belongeth to Zidon, and dwell there: behold, I have commanded a widow woman there to sustain thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 105,
            "text": "Luke 4:25 (25–26); Mosiah 21:10 (10, 17); Moro. 9:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:9",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "So he arose and went to Zarephath. And when he came to the gate of the city, behold, the widow woman was there gathering of sticks: and he called to her, and said, Fetch me, I pray thee, a little water in a vessel, that I may drink.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 104
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 17:10",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 17,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And as she was going to fetch it, he called to her, and said, Bring me, I pray thee, a morsel of bread in thine hand.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "Alma 8:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 8:20.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 8:20",
            "references": [
